          </constraints>
        </categoryLink>
        <categoryLink name="Flagship" id="ca49-e5b1-b95d-c847" hidden="false" targetId="0ec6-f5c8-25d7-89d8" tracked="true">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="3a43-c098-edfb-ef21" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="3"/>
          </constraints>
        </categoryLink>
      </categoryLinks>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Strategic Vantage" id="91f5-e051-fcd8-a8e6" hidden="false">
          <description>When Determining Initiative at the start of the game, the Battlefleet’s Admiral can draw two Victory &amp; Valour Cards, look at both, then place one of them back on top of the deck. The remaining card is revealed and used to determine which Admiral may choose to claim the Initiative.

If there is a tie, this Admiral may again draw two cards, repeating the process until one player reveals a card with the highest Value.

Additionally, when Determining Initiative in the Ready Phase of subsequent Rounds, if this Battlefleet’s Admiral decides to Hold Their Nerve, they can draw two Bonus Cards instead of one.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </forceEntry>
