                <rule name="IN TREUE FEST" id="efe5-574d-ea5b-5f9a" hidden="false">
                  <description>This Doctrine can only be purchased for a Bavarian Flagship unit.

Whenever a Bavarian Airborne model in this Force is targeted by an Attack action, this Force’s Admiral can make a Crew Check for the target. 

If successful, the model gains the Evasive property until the end of the current activation.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="MODULAR CONFIGURATION" id="1273-dca4-d881-8057" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="8" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="eee8-87db-90c2-9893" automatic="false" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Points" typeId="89fa-eeaa-958f-ca32" value="20"/>
                <cost name="VP per Model" typeId="c245-c6fc-adb8-407a" value="0"/>
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule name="MODULAR CONFIGURATION" id="e259-08a2-aaba-0c43" hidden="false">
                  <description>This Doctrine can only be purchased for a Imperium Flagship unit. 


At the start of their turn in the Make a Special Deployment Action step of Deployment, this Admiral can nominate one of their units in the Play Area that contains at least one Modular model. 


Each Modular model in the unit can exchange any Light or Heavy Hardpoint Weapons for a different weapon option that could have been selected for that Hardpoint during Force Selection. 


A Generator Hardpoint cannot be swapped in or out in this way.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
